{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-21T10:55:01.933Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented append-only interactive planning telemetry and an observed-only harness usage port.\n\n**Core**\n- New `src/core/planning.ts`: `plan_started`/`plan_exited` record types, `NULL_PLANNING_USAGE`, exact-bytes brief SHA-256, osq version resolution, `recordPlanStarted`/`recordPlanExited`, `readPlanningUsage` (absence/throw → all-null), and defensive `parsePlanRecords`/`readPlanRecords`/`correlatePlanSessions`/`readPlanningSessions` for later manifest/show/report reuse.\n\n**Harness port**\n- `src/harness/types.ts`: `InteractiveUsage`, `ReadInteractiveUsageOptions`, optional `readInteractiveUsage`.\n- `opencode-usage.ts`: selects one `session` row via `db --format json` by cwd + observed interval, sums stored cache-read/write, no messages read.\n- `codex-usage.ts`: resolves `CODEX_HOME`/`~/.codex`, matches one new rollout by `session_meta.payload.cwd`, maps last `thread_token_usage`, `cost: null`.\n- `agy.ts`: explicit all-null reader; timing still exact.\n- Adapters delegate; no adapter estimates or picks among multiple candidates.\n\n**CLI**\n- `src/cli/plan.ts` records the correlated pair around the existing spawn, calls the reader only after the child closes, and preserves non-zero propagation. `-print` is untouched.\n\n**Tests/fixtures**\n- `tests/plan-telemetry.test.ts` (15 tests) plus `tests/fixtures/planning/{fake-planner.mjs, opencode-session.json, codex-rollout.jsonl}` cover ordering, pairing, wall time, all three harness identities, exact usage mapping, ambiguity/malformed/failure nulls, resume, print mode, and hash independence.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/plan-telemetry.test.ts` → 15/15 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` → exit 0.\n\nResults written to `openspec/changes/035-planning-telemetry-and-cycle-time/.run/results/1.md`. Note: two pre-existing `tests/delta-merge.test.ts` failures (cli-foundation ownership glob vs HEAD) are unrelated; they aren't part of `pnpm verify` because that script's glob only matches nested tests."}}
